According to a new report from Intel Market Research, the global Liquid Nitrogen Atmospheric Pressure Storage Tank Market was valued at USD 185 million in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 254 million by 2034, delivering a compound annual growth rate of approximately 4.3% over the forecast horizon. This growth reflects heightened adoption across biotechnology and semiconductor segments and a revised CAGR that captures the accelerating demand dynamics inherent to these industries.
Liquid‑nitrogen atmospheric‑pressure storage tanks are cryogenic vessels engineered to safely contain liquid nitrogen at ambient pressure while preserving its ultra‑low temperature of –196 °C. These containers combine high‑strength alloys-typically stainless steel or aluminum-with cutting‑edge multi‑layer vacuum insulation or advanced polyurethane foam cores, thereby minimizing boil‑off losses and eliminating pressure buildup during storage or transport.
